NEW
- Fungi Mystery Season. Join our heroes in the dizzy and unpredictable joyride to the vibrant magical forest full of fluorescent mushrooms, moth maidens, fractals, and mind-bending weapons
- Mysterious Shining event. Dive into the third chapter of our story-driven Intriguing Wandering quest. Gear up to save the pixel Earth and claim a new gun, gadget, and tons of other prizes
- Forest Clash event. Test your skills in this intense competitive challenge. The rules are simple: the more enemies you destroy, the more rewards you earn. So keep your finger on the trigger
- Moth Queen Lottery. Experience true royal offerings from another world. Love moths and butterflies? With these guns, you will!
- Green Restoration Set. Show your eco-conscious side with an avatar, pet, and heavy gun. A portion of the proceeds will be donated to charity

IMPROVEMENTS
- Personal Events. New personalized quests for pixelgunners looking to score extra rewards
- Map Rotation

BUG FIXES
Fixed critical damage mechanics not working correctly when headshot didn't count;
Fixed the bug with overlaying interface in a clan lobby when viewing requests to join;
Fixed the bug with overlaying interface in a clan profile;
Fixed abuse mechanics on iOS when rerolling a super chest;
Steam version, Raids mode - fixed a bug where match statistics could not be viewed by pressing the Tab key;
Fixed the bug with auto-shooting not working at the boss on level 4, world 3 campaign;
Fixed the bug with resetting progress in the Lucky Board when switching between mobile and Steam platforms;
Fixed the bug related to the increase of gravity force depending on the frame rate;
Fixed the Battle Kusarigama weapon’s boomerang mechanics when the projectile goes through walls;
Fixed the description of the requirement to collect more stars to open a new map in the company;
Fixed the bug where the barrel of the Mutagen Neutralizer weapon was rotating when the character was moving;
Fixed the Curious Detective avatar texture bug;
Fixed the bug with duplicate weapon numbers in the gallery.

Hey, Pixelgunners!

In update 24.6 for Pixel Gun 3D: PC Edition, we've added:

— A new reporting system – send us a note about unfair players quickly and efficiently without quitting the match;
—  Steam achievements;
—  A more convenient and user-friendly Event Center;
—  An improved clan search system;
—  Improved Clan War registration;
—  Minor tweaks to Tournament mode based on your feedback.

And, as per tradition, we have rotated the maps and fixed small but pesky bugs.

Additionally, this update paves the way for all major activities: a nostalgic new Pixel Pass season, wild new Sets and Lottery, and the Project Task event where you can win rewards created by your fellow Pixelgunners! All this and more are coming soon!

Check out all the changes and improvements now!

[img]{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/44453777/f46a5c36652ad0dc837b1ce6feed436ebd661ba8.png[/img]

Great celebrations require preparations.

By downloading update 24.4, you confirm that you're ready:

- for the new Tournament season;
- to help the heroes in their final battle with Portalius;
- to meet characters both old and new;
- to add new guns, pets, and other useful items to your Armory;
- for a massive celebration of Pixel Gun 3D's 11th birthday.

The update you CANNOT miss!

[img]{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/44453777/0c16d0c3f321135eb69e9cd4dcf35ca72b7775bf.png[/img]

Hey, pixelgunners!

Before we roll out the significant patch addressing key requests – like enabling custom key mapping and enhancing gamepad connectivity – we launch a smaller update to boost server stability and iron out the little bugs. You can now enjoy the following enhancements:
[list]
[*] Improved gamepad recognition on handheld consoles;
[*] GamepadManager refactor ensuring more reliable gamepad controls;
[*] An option to toggle Chromatic Aberration on or off.
[*] Game volume control in the control tutorial;
[*] Ability to mute the sound on the queue screen;
[*] Fixed scoreboard on gamepads.
[/list]
To know the score of all the updates, patches, rebalance news, and giveaways for the PC Edition, follow our Events & Announcements on the Steam page.

[img]{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/44453777/0266f8f81f2d52c506a06fa835af2444e8d5b17f.png[/img]

Hello, pixelgunners!

We want to express our gratitude for your continued support. Your feedback has been instrumental in helping us identify problematic areas, and we are committed to fixing them as quickly as possible. Recently, we released patch 24.3.8, which included several improvements, and we have another patch set to be released this week that will:

[list]
[*] Add key mapping for the keyboard;
[*] Disable movement while the scoreboard is open;
[*] Add the ability to mute the sound on the queue screen;
[*] Add the ability to adjust the application volume in the control tutorial.
[/list]
In addition to these main improvements, we will fix several small bugs that may have been causing issues.
We are always working to improve the PC Edition to make your gaming experience as comfortable as possible. We will keep you updated on all the changes in separate news. Thank you again for your support!
